course: dictionary
lesson: 5508
title: Laziness and context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Laziness is a noun. It names not wanting to work or make an effort, even when you are able to. Look at the words around it to check. In «Laziness rarely hurts only the lazy one», the clue is hurts: laziness can cause harm to other people too.
explain: Context helps you tell laziness apart from other things. «Depression is an illness, not laziness, and doctors can help.» A person who is ill cannot simply decide to try harder, so the sentence shows that illness is not laziness.
explain: Stories often show laziness as a fault. In «The Ant and the Grasshopper», the grasshopper plays all summer and has nothing ready for winter. Teachers praise effort rather than talent to help pupils avoid laziness.
fact: Laziness means not wanting to work or make an effort, even when you are able to.
fact: Laziness is uncountable, so say «pure laziness», not «a laziness».
fact: «Out of laziness» means someone did not try because they could not be bothered.
fact: Being tired or ill is different from laziness, and rest is needed.
fact: «Signed off» means a doctor has said someone cannot work for now, and it is part of getting better, not laziness.
exercise: What does laziness mean? | Feeling sad after a long day | *Not wanting to work or make an effort, even when able | Loving to read books | Being unable to walk because of an injury
exercise: In «The Ant and the Grasshopper», the grasshopper plays all summer. What is the story showing? | Playing is always the best choice | *Laziness is a fault and can cause trouble later | Winter is the best season of the year | Ants are lazy and unkind
exercise: Which phrase shows someone did not try because they could not be bothered? | Out of tune | *Out of laziness | Out of sight | Out of date
test: «In teenagers the body clock shifts later, so they feel sleepy late and hate mornings: partly biology, not just laziness.» What does this suggest about sleepy teenagers? | *Their tiredness is partly biology, not only laziness | Mornings are the best time to sleep | Body clocks never change at all | They are always lazy and should get up earlier
test: Which sentence uses laziness correctly? | *The teacher spoke about laziness in the class meeting | The teacher spoke about the lazy in the class meeting | The teacher spoke about lazinesses in the class meeting | The teacher spoke about a laziness in the class meeting
exam: «Laziness rarely hurts only the lazy one.» What does this sentence suggest? | Laziness always makes people happy | Laziness is good for everyone | *Laziness can affect other people too | Laziness only hurts the person who is lazy
